      "gold_resolved": true,
      "status": "answered",
      "answer_text": "The incident report links the six‑hour PaymentService timeout to the **auth‑gateway** deployment (08:10 UTC) [S1].  Operations later identified the root cause as a **mis‑configured JWT TTL** on AuthGateway that triggered cascading retries into PaymentService [S3].  However, the release notes for the same auth‑gateway version (2.4.1, deployed at 14:00 UTC) attribute the outage to a **Neon connection‑pool exhaustion**, explicitly stating it was not a JWT‑TTL issue [S2].  The service‑component guide also advises checking Neon pool metrics when the service fails [S4].  \n\n**Contradictions:**  \n- Deploy time: 08:10 UTC (incident report) vs 14:00 UTC (change log) [S1][S2].  \n- Root‑cause attribution: ops claim (JWT TTL) vs release notes (Neon pool exhaustion) [S3][S2].",
